34,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"It seems usage is heavily skewed toward those closest to the door, and cleaning is an unfair burden.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,We lack a private space for meaningful or difficult dialogue. We are becoming strangers in our own office.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,We're spending a lot of time walking for lunch and paying for outside rooms for tiny meetings. It's a waste.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"We've spent 68,000 yen on outside hires for small groups. A meeting fit-out is 141,000, but it pays for itself.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,The walls are thin; we hear everything. And the crumbs at our desks prove we need a dedicated place to eat.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If we make it a kitchen, the cleaning issue will only worsen, as seen with the old fridge.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"A kitchen is social, but a meeting space provides the privacy we currently lack for sensitive talks.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,Twenty-five minutes for lunch is a lot of lost time. A kitchen would be a huge quality-of-life win.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"A kitchen is cheaper to install, but a meeting space solves the external cost leak. We need to be pragmatic.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"A quiet room might solve the noise, but it doesn't solve the crumbs or the lack of connection.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A meeting space with a calendar would solve the ""first come, first served"" unfairness I noticed in the tally.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Ryuji. A bookable space ensures everyone has access and provides the necessary privacy.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"But who is going to clean the meeting room? If it's a kitchen, we can just manage our own food.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the meeting room is just a table and a screen. A kitchen requires an electrician and constant upkeep.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,We must balance the need for nourishment with the need for professional privacy.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,The data suggests a meeting space is the most equitable and least messy option.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,It is the only option that addresses the emotional distance and the lack of private communication.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"I still think the lunch commute is a nightmare, but I see the point about the cleaning.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,The numbers favor the meeting space if we want to stop paying outside hire fees. It's the logical choice.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"If the walls are thin, a dedicated meeting space with a proper door and schedule is best.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
